<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nelson Mandela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/2013">2013</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nelson Mandela was a South African anti-apartheid leader born into a junior branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thembu">Thembu</a> royal house. A leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a>, he was imprisoned from 1962 to 1990. After negotiating the end of apartheid he became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s first democratically elected president in 1994, serving until 1999, and shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela.jpg" alt="Nelson Mandela" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kingkongphoto &amp; www.celebrity-photos.com from Laurel · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nelson_Mandela_1994.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
